s{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/deployments","created_at":"2012-12-07T13:30:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T11:48:01Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-11T20:11:30Z","git_url":"git://github.com/python/mypy.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:python/mypy.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy","homepage":"https://www.mypy-lang.org/","size":77161,"stargazers_count":20064,"watchers_count":20064,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":3065,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3124,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/pulls/7878","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/7878","diff_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/7878.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/7878.patch","merged_at":"2019-11-06T17:07:34Z"},"body":"This PR aims to support negative int Literal, resolves #7844 \r\n\r\n~Currently, the newly added test will broke and show inconsistent output with directly invoking mypy from command line~\r\n\r\nCommit 278ec69 shows the inconsistent error output between running mypy from command line and running from tests\r\n\r\nCommit 7b3d1e8 now behaves ideally for testcase like #7844. But it breaks current codebase and tests.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/7878/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/7878/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/549649096","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/7844#issuecomment-549649096","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/7844","id":549649096,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0OTY0OTA5Ng==","user":{"login":"TH3CHARLie","id":22651013,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjUxMDEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22651013?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie","html_url":"https://github.com/TH3CHARLie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-11-05T03:36:30Z","updated_at":"2019-11-05T06:50:10Z","body":"@Michael0x2a I have started a PR for this issue. I have finished the callback function but the test keeps failing and  it produces output shown below\r\n```\r\n# test code \r\n[case testNegativeIntLiteral]\r\nfrom typing_extensions import Literal\r\n\r\na: Literal[-2] = -2  # E: Incompatible types in assignment (expression has type \"int\", variable has type \"Literal[-2]\")\r\nb: Literal[-1] = -1  # E: Incompatible types in assignment (expression has type \"int\", variable has type \"Literal[-1]\")\r\nc: Literal[0] = 0\r\nd: Literal[1] = 1\r\ne: Literal[2] = 2\r\n[out]\r\n\r\n# output\r\nExpected:\r\n  main:3: error: Incompatible types in assignment (expression has type \"int\", variable has type \"Literal[-2]\") (diff)\r\n  main:4: error: Incompatible types in assignment (expression has type \"int\", variable has type \"Literal[-1]\") (diff)\r\nActual:\r\n  main:3: error: Unsupported operand type for unary - (\"int\") (diff)\r\n  main:4: error: Unsupported operand type for unary - (\"int\") (diff)\r\n```\r\nHowever,  invoking mypy directly from the command line does produce errors like @crusaderky 's code did. So I decided to only commit my test for now and maybe we should investigate this inconsistency first. See commit 278ec69.\r\n\r\nI follow the above guidance by adding a new method callback for `builtins.int.__neg__`, see commit 7b3d1e8, it now behaves ideally for testcase discussed in this issue. But it breaks current codebase and tests. For example, see  assignment at https://github.com/python/mypy/blob/3fc382321e4531450e91c55fddb6d4ed54611d5e/mypy/subtypes.py#L375 and its declaration https://github.com/python/mypy/blob/3fc382321e4531450e91c55fddb6d4ed54611d5e/mypy/subtypes.py#L360\r\nProduced error output for this commit\r\n```\r\nmypy/subtypes.py:375: error: Incompatible types in assignment (expression has type \"int\", variable has type \"Literal[-1]\")  [assignment]\r\n                                previous_match_left_index = left_index\r\n```\r\n\r\nAdd explicit `int` type annotations can solve this, but this requires changing lots of sources and tests.\r\n\r\nThat's what I have finished so far, and I may need some guidance from here.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/549649096/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"TH3CHARLie","id":22651013,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjUxMDEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22651013?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie","html_url":"https://github.com/TH3CHARLie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TH3CHARLie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":2769981829,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50Mjc2OTk4MTgyOQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/2769981829","actor":{"login":"Michael0x2a","id":1424628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjQ2Mjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1424628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a","html_url":"https://github.com/Michael0x2a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.git